  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 · Governed knowledge before AI",
      "items": [
        "Source acquisition, parsing, normalization, content versioning, governance refresh and chunking are deterministic application/domain concerns.",
        "SQLite is the current durable local/test baseline; production Postgres remains planned rather than implied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "2 · Retrieval strategies stay separable",
      "items": [
        "BM25 preserves exact-term and identifier behavior; dense retrieval uses exact cosine to isolate representation quality before ANN complexity.",
        "Hybrid V1 uses Reciprocal Rank Fusion because BM25 and cosine scores do not share a calibrated raw-score scale."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "3 · Stable evidence outside the model",
      "items": [
        "Generated artifacts persist stable EvidenceRef objects. Temporary E1..EN aliases exist only inside one model invocation.",
        "Exact alias resolution proves reference validity, not semantic entailment; semantic support is evaluated separately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "4 · Capabilities own business semantics",
      "items": [
        "Resolve owns Knowledge Article and service-resolution policy; Training owns procedure-generation semantics.",
        "LangChain is an adapter for structured model execution, not the owner of authorization, evidence identity, lifecycle or evaluation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "5 · Quality is layered",
      "items": [
        "Software CI, retrieval evaluation, grounded-generation evaluation and product outcome evaluation are distinct evidence layers.",
        "ANN/HNSW, durable workflow orchestration and hosted observability remain deferred until measured requirements justify them."
      ]
    }
  ]
